==Strategy==
This stage introduces Prof. Owlbrowley, who is like [[Owlbrow]] but with longer range and an extremely annoying Freeze effect. The good news is that they're both [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], meaning both [[Fishman Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]] can jump them.

In this stage specifically, it's pretty hard to actually hit Owlbrowley with those counters given the frontline enemies, so use methods of pierce like [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] to chip them down. [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]] deals with Miz Devil, Talented [[Pizza Cat]] can occasionally do a high-damage [[Wave Attack|Wave]] while fighting Bun Bun Black, and [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]'s [[Surge Attack|Surges]] not only do heavy damage to Le'Behemoth and Miz Devil, but also hit Owlbrowley. Add [[Barrel Cat]] for Le'Behemoth, [[Can Can Cat]] for Dogenstein, and a backliner like [[Awakened Urs]] and this stage should be done without much issue.

==Trivia==
*Incompetent Watchman's Japanese name, 万人通す番人 ''Ban'nin Tōsu Ban'nin'' ("Guard Who Lets Everyone Pass"), plays off of how 万人 ("everyone") and 番人 ("watchman" or "guard") are both pronounced ''ban'nin''.

